From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Kleinschmidt <jkleinsc@electronjs.org>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 10:08:46 -0400
Subject: fix: do not pass removed JSPI V8 flag

Chromium's V8 enables JSPI by default and removed the experimental flag,
while Node.js v24.20 passes it unconditionally. Remove the obsolete argument
so Node startup and snapshot generation work with Chromium's V8.

This patch can be removed once Node.js no longer passes the removed flag.

Refs: https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/59941
Refs: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/6937664

diff --git a/src/node.cc b/src/node.cc
index d7fa3d8fdf23610917723b0bb808e19adc002f76..eb8835d5e66c67d6727ef75636770c7cd7c27930 100644
--- a/src/node.cc
+++ b/src/node.cc
@@ -790,11 +790,6 @@ static ExitCode ProcessGlobalArgsInternal(std::vector<std::string>* args,
     v8_args.emplace_back("--js-source-phase-imports");
   }
 
-#if V8_ENABLE_WEBASSEMBLY
-  // WebAssembly JS Promise Integration
-  v8_args.emplace_back("--experimental-wasm-jspi");
-#endif  // V8_ENABLE_WEBASSEMBLY
-
 #ifdef __POSIX__
   // Block SIGPROF signals when sleeping in epoll_wait/kevent/etc.  Avoids the
   // performance penalty of frequent EINTR wakeups when the profiler is running.
